x496 text "The primer"
x497 puts x495 x496
x498 call close x497 
x499 call open x498 2
x500 write x499 2
x501 text "This is everything a model is told before it writes or edits A0. The sections below say the same thing in full."
x502 puts x500 x501
x503 call close x502 
x504 call open x503 10
x505 write x504 4
x506 write x505 2
x507 text "code wrap"
x508 puts x506 x507
x509 call open x508 4
x510 write x509 2
x511 text "A0: `fn NAME T... -> T`, lines `ID OP ARG...`, `ret ARG` (or `ret OP ARGS`), `end`. Types u32 bool, arrays u32x4, records (u32,bool). Params p0 p1... Args: earlier ID, pN, u32 literal, true, false. Ops exact mod 2^32.\n"
x512 puts x510 x511
x513 write x512 2
x514 text "mov add sub mul | and or xor (u32 bitwise, or bool logical) | shl shr (count&31) | div (b=0: 4294967295) rem (b=0: a) | eq ne (u32 or bool) lt le gt ge (unsigned) -> bool | select c x y\n"
x515 puts x513 x514
x516 write x515 2
x517 text "call F a... | fold F n s a... state=s; i<n: state=F(state,i,a...)\n"
x518 puts x516 x517
x519 write x518 2
x520 text "arr e... | rec e... | get a i (i mod N) | set a i v | at r k | put r k v (values, no aliasing)\n"
x521 puts x519 x520
x522 write x521 2
x523 text "EDIT: reply bare edit lines (handle line optional when one e handle is shown), e.g. `c add a b` (replaces c or inserts before ret; `c add a b @ x` inserts after x), `-c`, `ret c`, `fn f u32 -> u32` then lines, `ret`, `end` (adds/replaces a function), `-fn f`.\n"
x524 puts x522 x523
x525 call close x524 
x526 call close x525 
x527 call close x526 
x528 call open x527 13
x529 write x528 4
x530 write x529 1
x531 text "programs"
x532 puts x530 x531
x533 call open x532 11
x534 write x533 2
x535 text "Programs and functions"
x536 puts x534 x535
x537 call close x536 
x538 call open x537 2
x539 write x538 2
x540 text "A program is a list of functions. A function is a header `fn NAME T... -> T`, then one instruction per line `ID OP ARGS`, then `ret ARG` (or `ret OP ARGS`, which names a fresh node), then `end`. Names are lowercase identifiers. Parameters are p0, p1, ... in header order. An argument is an earlier ID in the same function, a parameter, a u32 literal, true, or false. There are no forward references, no recursion, and no nested expressions."
x541 puts x539 x540
x542 call close x541 
x543 call open x542 10
x544 write x543 4
x545 write x544 2
x546 text "code"
x547 puts x545 x546
x548 call open x547 4
x549 call open x548 6
x550 write x549 4
x551 write x550 2
x552 text "cm"
x553 puts x551 x552
x554 write x553 2
x555 text "# clamp p0 into [p1, p2]\n"
x556 puts x554 x555
x557 call close x556 
x558 write x557 2
x559 text "fn clamp u32 u32 u32 -> u32\nlo lt p0 p1\nhi lt p2 p0\na select lo p1 p0\nr select hi p2 a\nret r\nend"
x560 puts x558 x559
x561 call close x560 
x562 call close x561 
x563 call close x562 
x564 call open x563 13
x565 write x564 4
x566 write x565 1
x567 text "types"
x568 puts x566 x567
x569 call open x568 11
x570 write x569 2
x571 text "Types and values"
x572 puts x570 x571
x573 call close x572 
x574 call open x573 2
x575 write x574 2
x576 text "u32 is an exact 32-bit unsigned integer; every arithmetic result wraps modulo 2^32. bool is true or false, never a number. Arrays u32xN and records (T,T,...) are values: get, set, at, and put return a copy, they never alias. io is a linear token, meaning every io value is used exactly once; that is what makes output order checkable."
x577 puts x575 x576
x578 call close x577 
x579 call close x578 
x580 call open x579 13
x581 write x580 4
x582 write x581 1
x583 text "iteration"
x584 puts x582 x583
x585 call open x584 11
x586 write x585 2
x587 text "Iteration"
x588 puts x586 x587
x589 call close x588 
x590 call open x589 2
x591 write x590 2
x592 text "A function body has no loops. Repetition is fold and loop over an earlier function: the step function receives the state, the index, and any extra arguments, and returns the next state. loop adds a predicate function that is checked before each iteration. A literal count is checked against a per-function budget when the program is checked. A variable count is bounded by fuel (a step budget) in the reference interpreter, the plain slow implementation that every target is compared with; compiled targets have no execution budget."
x593 puts x591 x592
x594 call close x593 
x595 call open x594 10
x596 write x595 4
x597 write x596 2
x598 text "code"
x599 puts x597 x598
x600 call open x599 4
x601 call open x600 6
x602 write x601 4
x603 write x602 2
x604 text "cm"
x605 puts x603 x604
x606 write x605 2
x607 text "# sum of squares 0..n-1 with fold; the step is an earlier function\n"
x608 puts x606 x607
x609 call close x608 
x610 write x609 2
x611 text "fn sqstep u32 u32 -> u32\ns mul p1 p1\nr add p0 s\nret r\nend\nfn sumsq -> u32\nr fold sqstep 10 0\nret r\nend"
x612 puts x610 x611
x613 call close x612 
x614 call close x613 
x615 call close x614 
x616 call open x615 13
x617 write x616 4
x618 write x617 1
x619 text "modules"
x620 puts x618 x619
x621 call open x620 11
x622 write x621 2
x623 text "Modules"
x624 puts x622 x623
x625 call close x624 
x626 call open x625 2
x627 write x626 2
x628 text "A file starts with zero or more `use \"path.a0\"` lines, relative to the file. The linker loads every used file once, orders them by dependency, and checks the result as one program with one namespace. Cycles and duplicate function names are rejected, and diagnostics name the file and line."
x629 puts x627 x628
x630 call close x629 
x631 call open x630 10
x632 write x631 4
x633 write x632 2
x634 text "code"
x635 puts x633 x634
x636 call open x635 4
x637 write x636 2
x638 text "use \"ui.a0\"\nuse \"../examples/life.a0\"\nfn page io -> io\na call open p0 5\nb call close a\nret b\nend"
x639 puts x637 x638
x640 call close x639 
x641 call close x640 
x642 call close x641 
ret x642
end

