x655 write x654 2
x656 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0), one signature line per callee, and a program handle (g0). The program view is scoped to the target, its transitive callees and its direct callers, so it stays the same size as the program grows. The revision is a short hash of the program text; an edit written against an older revision is rejected rather than applied to code that has moved. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line, as in the quick start."
x657 puts x655 x656
x658 call close x657 
x659 call open x658 10
x660 write x659 4
x661 write x660 2
x662 text "code"
x663 puts x661 x662
x664 call open x663 4
x665 call open x664 6
x666 write x665 4
x667 write x666 2
x668 text "cm"
x669 puts x667 x668
x670 write x669 2
x671 text "# a view of clamp, then a reply that fixes the upper bound\n"
x672 puts x670 x671
x673 call close x672 
x674 write x673 2
x675 text "e0 fn clamp u32 u32 u32 -> u32\nlo lt p0 p1\nhi lt p2 p0\na select lo p1 p0\nr select hi p2 a\nret r\n\n"
x676 puts x674 x675
x677 call open x676 6
x678 write x677 4
x679 write x678 2
x680 text "cm"
x681 puts x679 x680
x682 write x681 2
x683 text "# reply\n"
x684 puts x682 x683
x685 call close x684 
x686 write x685 2
x687 text "e0\nhi lt p2 a\nr select hi p2 a"
x688 puts x686 x687
x689 call close x688 
x690 call close x689 
x691 call close x690 
x692 call open x691 13
x693 write x692 4
x694 write x693 1
x695 text "diagnostics"
x696 puts x694 x695
x697 call open x696 11
x698 write x697 2
x699 text "Diagnostics"
x700 puts x698 x699
x701 call close x700 
x702 call open x701 2
x703 write x702 2
x704 text "Every rejection carries a stable code (parse, type, structure, handle, revision, limit), what was expected, what was seen, and the one fix that resolves it. The compiler never guesses: an ambiguous reply is rejected with the fix, not applied approximately."
x705 puts x703 x704
x706 call close x705 
x707 call close x706 
ret x707
end

